@@ -200,6 +200,34 @@ The following arguments are supported:
 
 The middleware won't GZip responses that already have a `Content-Encoding` set, to prevent them from being encoded twice.
 
+## RequestBodyLimitMiddleware
+
+Buffers HTTP request bodies before calling the application and rejects bodies
+that exceed a byte limit. It counts actual received bytes regardless of the
+`Content-Length` header.
+
+```python
+from starlette.applications import Starlette
+from starlette.middleware import Middleware
+from starlette.middleware.body_limit import RequestBodyLimitMiddleware
+
+
+routes = ...
+middleware = [Middleware(RequestBodyLimitMiddleware, max_bytes=1024 * 1024)]
+app = Starlette(routes=routes, middleware=middleware)
+```
+
+`max_bytes` is required and must be `None` or a non-negative integer. Invalid
+values, including booleans, raise `ValueError` at construction. `None` disables
+buffering and the limit. A zero limit accepts empty bodies.
+
+Oversize requests receive a plain-text `413` response with the body
+`Request body too large`. The middleware stops reading at the first crossing
+and does not call the application. Accepted bodies are replayed to the
+application, supporting normal body and JSON caching. Subsequent receive calls
+are delegated to the original stream. WebSocket and lifespan scopes pass
+through without buffering.
+
 ## BaseHTTPMiddleware
 
 An abstract class that allows you to write ASGI middleware against a request/response
